  "main_hypothesis": {
    "hypothesis": "The matched 0.75-times-viscosity candidate_6073 lies between candidate_5908, which completed all conditions but was underdamped, and candidate_5610, which settled kinematically but retained loaded static-balance failures; therefore candidate_6073 may preserve unloaded qualification and improve loaded settling enough to reduce or clear the complete frozen-task violation without the high-viscosity unloaded static-balance failure observed at candidate_5745.",
    "expected_observation": "All ten frozen load conditions integrate completely with legal routes, no contacts or warnings, qualified unloaded windows, and improved loaded qualification relative to candidate_5908. The decisive observation is the exact original evaluator outcome and per-condition qualification: ideally every loaded window clears static balance, speed, qvel, drift and length-excess thresholds and all 251 task constraints pass; otherwise the pattern and magnitude of failures will locate the remaining viscosity tradeoff.",
    "weakening_observation": "Failure of unloaded dynamic qualification, incomplete integration, route/contact defects, or loaded speed, qvel, drift or length-excess failures comparable to candidate_5908 would weaken the intermediate-viscosity hypothesis. Persistent static-balance-only failures comparable to candidate_5610 would show that this viscosity edit does not resolve the dominant late-window defect. Any original task-constraint failure refutes complete-task success for this candidate."
